law.text:
		The Board shall make, adopt, and promulgate regulations governing the following aspects of private management and operation of regional jail facilities approved by the General Assembly pursuant to § 53.1-71.4:

Minimum standards for the construction, equipment, administration, and operation of the facilities; however, the standards shall be at least as stringent as those established for local correctional facilities;


Contingency plans for operation of a contractor-operated facility in the event of a termination of the contract;


Use of deadly and nondeadly force by regional jail facility contractors' security personnel;


Methods of monitoring a contractor-operated facility by an appropriate state or local governmental entity or entities;


Public access to a contractor-operated facility; and


Such other regulations as may be necessary to carry out the provisions of this article.
